## Pusher Channel Strategy

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Channels"
        C1["private-restaurant-{restaurantId}"]
        C2["private-order-{orderId}"]
    end

    subgraph "Client Events (P2P — no backend)"
        E1["client-driver-location<br/>{driverId, lat, lng, bearing, timestamp}"]
        E2["client-request-location<br/>(user asks driver where are you?)"]
    end

    subgraph "Server Events (backend triggers)"
        E3["delivery-assigned<br/>{orderId, driverId, driverName}"]
        E4["delivery-status-update<br/>{orderId, status, timestamp}"]
        E5["driver-status-change<br/>{driverId, status}"]
    end

    C1 --- E1
    C1 --- E3
    C1 --- E4
    C1 --- E5
    C2 --- E1
    C2 --- E2
    C2 --- E4
```

**Who subscribes to what:**

| Subscriber | Channel | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Branch Dashboard | `private-restaurant-{restaurantId}` | See ALL drivers + ALL delivery updates |
| User (tracking) | `private-order-{orderId}` | See only THEIR driver's location + delivery status |
| Driver App | `private-restaurant-{restaurantId}` + `private-order-{orderId}` per active delivery | Send location to both channels |

**Driver with multiple deliveries:**
```
Driver subscribes to:
  private-restaurant-{restaurantId}     ← always (1 channel)
  private-order-{orderId1}              ← active delivery 1
  private-order-{orderId2}              ← active delivery 2

Each location update → send client-driver-location to ALL subscribed channels
When delivery 1 completed → unsubscribe from private-order-{orderId1}
```

### Pusher Free Tier Capacity

```
V1 (1 restaurant, 3 drivers, 15 deliveries/day):
  Location: 2,700 messages/day
  Status + orders: ~240 messages/day
  TOTAL: ~2,940 messages/day

  FREE TIER LIMIT: 200,000 messages/day
  USAGE: 1.5% ← VERY SAFE ✅
  
  Connections: ~8 (limit: 100) ✅
  Channels: ~5 (limit: 200) ✅
```

