## Edge Cases & Solutions

### Edge Case 1: User Opens Tracking Page Late

**Problem:** Driver has been delivering for 10 minutes. User opens tracking — no location history since we don't save to DB. User sees blank map until next Pusher event (5-30 seconds).

**Solution: "Request Location" Ping**
```
User opens tracking page
  → subscribes to private-order-{orderId}
  → sends client event: "client-request-location"

Driver app listens for "client-request-location"
  → immediately responds with current GPS position
  → User sees driver within 1-2 seconds ✅
```

### Edge Case 2: Driver Goes Offline / Loses Internet

**Solution:**
```
User frontend tracks "lastUpdateTimestamp":
  < 30 seconds ago  → Green "Live" badge
  30s - 2 min ago   → Yellow "Updating..." badge  
  > 2 minutes ago   → Red "Driver may be offline" badge

When driver reconnects:
  → Pusher SDK auto-reconnects (built-in exponential backoff)
  → Next GPS position sent immediately
  → Map resumes tracking seamlessly
```

### Edge Case 3: Driver App Goes to Background / Screen Off

**Problem:** Mobile browsers restrict GPS when tab is in background.

**V1 Solution (testing):**
- Show warning: "Keep this tab active for location tracking"
- Use `document.visibilitychange` to detect background
- When foregrounded, immediately send current position

**V2 Solution (production):**
- Convert to PWA with service worker for background geolocation
- Or build React Native app

### Edge Case 4: Map Auto-Follow vs Free Pan

**Problem:** Should map auto-follow driver? What if user wants to zoom/pan?

**Solution:**
```
Default: Map auto-follows driver (keeps centered)
If user touches/drags/zooms map: Auto-follow PAUSES
Show floating "Re-center" button (like Google Maps)
Click re-center → resume auto-follow
```

### Edge Case 5: Pusher Connection Drops

**Problem:** Pusher has 99.997% uptime, but connections can drop on flaky networks.

**Solution:**
- Pusher JS SDK has built-in auto-reconnection
- During disconnect: UI shows "Reconnecting..." indicator (pulsing yellow)
- On reconnect: driver's next location update resumes tracking
- Status changes are DB-backed, so no data loss regardless

### Edge Case 6: Multiple Deliveries Per Driver

**Problem:** Driver has 3 orders. Needs to send location to 3 different order channels.

**Solution:** Driver subscribes to multiple order channels dynamically:
```
On new assignment → subscribe to private-order-{newOrderId}
On delivery complete → unsubscribe from private-order-{completedOrderId}
Location update → trigger client event on ALL subscribed channels
```

